   "source_number": "3.1.6",
   "kind": "exercise",
   "bloom": "Apply",
   "place": {
    "at": "end"
   },
   "cite": "carts-setup",
   "prompt": "<p>Suppose two masses on carts on frictionless surface are at displacements $\\kxone$ and $\\kxtwo$ as in Example 3.1.3. Suppose that a rocket applies force $F$ in the positive direction on cart $\\kxone$. Set up the system of equations.</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "open",
    "generated_by": "ai",
    "solution": "The rocket pushes only the first cart, so its force adds to the spring’s force $k(\\kxtwo - \\kxone)$ on that cart, and the second cart still feels only the spring. By Newton’s second law, $m_1\\kxonedprime = k(\\kxtwo - \\kxone) + F$, $m_2\\kxtwodprime = -k(\\kxtwo - \\kxone)$."
   }
  },
